  Top-level Structure

  - episodes: List of 146,304 navigation episodes (much larger than R2R)
  - instruction_vocab: Vocabulary dictionary with 2,504 words

  Individual Episode Structure

  Each episode contains the same structure as R2R:
  - episode_id: Unique identifier (integer)
  - trajectory_id: Trajectory identifier (integer)
  - scene_id: 3D scene identifier (string, format: "mp3d/{scene_id}/{scene_id}.glb")
  - start_position: Starting coordinates [x, y, z] (list of floats)
  - start_rotation: Starting orientation [x, y, z, w] (list of floats)
  - goals: Target position with radius (list of dict with 'position' and 'radius')
  - info: Additional metadata including 'geodesic_distance'
  - instruction: Navigation instruction containing:
    - instruction_text: Natural language instruction string
    - instruction_tokens: Tokenized instruction using vocabulary indices (with padding)
  - reference_path: Optimal path coordinates (list of [x, y, z] positions)

  Instruction Vocabulary

  - word_list: Complete vocabulary of 2,504 words
  - word2idx_dict: Word-to-index mapping
  - stoi: String-to-index mapping (same as word2idx_dict)
  - itos: Index-to-string mapping
  - num_vocab: Vocabulary size (2,504)
  - UNK_INDEX: Unknown token index (1)
  - PAD_INDEX: Padding token index (0)

  Sample Data

  - Instruction: "walk past the table and chairs and turn right . walk up the stairs and stop at the
  top of the stairs ."
  - Start position: [2.74, 0.09, -9.06]
  - Goal position: [4.86, 2.61, -10.89] (note: height change indicates multi-level navigation)
  - Geodesic distance: 10.45 meters
  - Reference path: 7 waypoints showing multi-level navigation

  Key Differences from R2R

  1. Much larger dataset: 146,304 episodes vs 10,819 in R2R
  2. Smaller vocabulary: 2,504 words vs 2,711 in R2R
  3. Longer instructions: Multi-sentence instructions with padding
  4. Multi-level navigation: Instructions involving stairs and elevation changes
  5. Structured vocabulary: Separate stoi/itos mappings plus UNK_INDEX/PAD_INDEX

  Dataset Statistics

  - Distance range: 3.46m - 30.71m (sampled from first 1,000 episodes)
  - Path length range: 5-7 waypoints (more consistent than R2R)
  - Scene coverage: Uses MP3D scenes like R2R

  The EnvDrop dataset appears to be an augmented or expanded version of R2R with more episodes,
  multi-level navigation scenarios, and structured tokenization with explicit padding and unknown
  token handling.
